      </g>

      <!-- LEO ground tracks: a satellite covers ~7.7 km/s, so at this frame's scale a
           pass streaks through in seconds, a few minutes apart. Track lines stay put,
           the way a real sat tracker draws them. Meteor-M N2-3/N2-4 descend near-polar
           (sun-synchronous) with a slight westward lean; the ISS crosses on its
